# "Sacrifice a creature": a creature you control, not any creature. Turn one: Altar off a Forest and two Moxen. Turn
# two: Bot2 casts an Ornithopter. Turn three: Bot1 controls no creature, so the Altar offers nothing (the refusal) even
# with Bot2's Ornithopter on the battlefield. Bot1 then casts its own Ornithopter - summoning sick, which does not matter
# for a cost that does not tap it - and the Altar, now offered, sacrifices it for {C}{C}. Bot2's Ornithopter stays.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Pearl
Mox Ruby
Ashnod's Altar
Ornithopter
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Ashnod's Altar.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
! Bot1.Battlefield.Ashnod's Altar.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
Bot1.Battlefield.Ashnod's Altar.Activate
? Bot1.Mana = {C}{C}

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Ornithopter
Bot2.Battlefield = Ornithopter
Bot1.Battlefield = Forest; Mox Pearl; Mox Ruby; Ashnod's Altar
